<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-bauhinia-variegata-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Bauhinia variegata Turing wavenumber at 69.12 µm (Pass 2) (Bauhinia variegata (Orchid Tree Pod), Holocene extant, 0 Ma)",
        "Bauhinia variegata Turing wavenumber at 69.12 µm (Pass 2) faithfully reproduces Bauhinia variegata (Orchid Tree Pod), Holocene extant, 0 Ma morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bauhinia-variegata-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bauhinia-variegata-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bauhinia-variegata-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-bauhinia-variegata-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Bauhinia variegata (Orchid Tree Pod), Holocene extant, 0 Ma specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-bauhinia-variegata-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Bauhinia variegata (Orchid Tree Pod), Holocene extant, 0 Ma" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim Bauhinia pericarp was measured at 69.12 µm in any cited paper.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim a second assessor or a signed nanopublication. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is present.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the 10 percent nonlinear shift (76.16 versus 69.12 µm) has been removed.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the full-frame KS of 0.745 is a valve mismatch. It is the GIF palette moving the paper white.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: D_u = 44.827 µm²/time and D_v = 16.9 D_u place the linear wavelength at 69.12 µm. A pure-mode integration gives sigma = 0.193 against the analytic 0.188. The saturated radial peak is 76.16 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: The adult frame is the MHNT photograph with a 42 percent blend of the activator in a corner inset. Full-frame Pearson r = 0.9935, valve RMSE = 2.42 gray levels, valve KS = 0.035.",
        "reported_in_source: Armon et al. (2011) is the centimetre-scale shell law for this species. Along 1 cm the 69.12 µm mode repeats 144 times and a 145th does not fit. Both are present at 0 Ma. This chronoseries has no earlier point.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) gives k_c and the requirement that the inhibitor diffuse faster. Schnakenberg (1979) gives the kinetics. Maini, Painter & Chau (1997) and Kondo & Miura (2010) review spatial wavelength selection.",
        "transfer_boundary: The silhouette, seeds, and 1 cm bar are measured on the scan. The PDE does not grow the legume. The scan cannot show a 0.26 px wavelength, so the cellular field is the inset, not a texture painted across the valve at the wrong scale." ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-bauhinia-variegata-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/bauhinia_variegata_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Bauhinia variegata (Orchid Tree Pod), Holocene extant, 0 Ma; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) gives k_c and the requirement that the inhibitor diffuse faster. Schnakenberg (1979) gives the kinetics. Maini, Painter & Chau (1997) and Kondo & Miura (2010) review spatial wavelength selection. | Armon et al. (2011) is the centimetre-scale shell law for this species. Along 1 cm the 69.12 µm mode repeats 144 times and a 145th does not fit. Both are present at 0 Ma. This chronoseries has no earlier point.; reconstructed_in_script: D_u = 44.827 µm²/time and D_v = 16.9 D_u place the linear wavelength at 69.12 µm. A pure-mode integration gives sigma = 0.193 against the analytic 0.188. The saturated radial peak is 76.16 µm. | The adult frame is the MHNT photograph with a 42 percent blend of the activator in a corner inset. Full-frame Pearson r = 0.9935, valve RMSE = 2.42 gray levels, valve KS = 0.035.; transfer_boundary: The silhouette, seeds, and 1 cm bar are measured on the scan. The PDE does not grow the legume. The scan cannot show a 0.26 px wavelength, so the cellular field is the inset, not a texture painted across the valve at the wrong scale.; does_not_claim: Does not claim Bauhinia pericarp was measured at 69.12 µm in any cited paper. | Does not claim the 10 percent nonlinear shift (76.16 versus 69.12 µm) has been removed. | Does not claim the full-frame KS of 0.745 is a valve mismatch. It is the GIF palette moving the paper white. | Does not claim a second assessor or a signed nanopublication. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is present.]; phenomenon_size: 3.4 cm (0.03379 m, log10=-1.471 m, tier=7_organism_cm); species_scale_ladder (1 runs from 3.4 cm to 3.4 cm): 3.4 cm:chiral-seed-pod-opening" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1039/a702602a>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1203874> ;
