<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bauhinia-variegata-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bauhinia variegata Turing wavenumber at 69.12 µm (Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 87.3/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the same species, the same age (0 Ma), and the same assigned scale (69.12 µm = 6.912e-05 m, log10 = -4.160). Diffusivity scaling now sets lambda in proportion to sqrt(D): 34.56, 48.88, 69.12, 97.75, 138.24 µm. The adult GIF frame blends the activator inset into the photograph and shares one palette, so full-frame Pearson r is 0.9935 (RMSE 8.75 gray levels). The valve-only KS is 0.035; the full-frame KS of 0.745 is the paper-white shift from GIF quantisation, reported separately. The 1 cm bar is 37 px, so 69.12 µm is 0.256 px. Equal diffusion remains stable (sigma_max = -0.1). The saturated radial peak is 76.16 µm, about 10 percent longer than the linear wavelength; that gap is reported rather than tuned away. Overall 87.3/100 (faithfulness 87.6, reproducibility 86.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/bauhinia_variegata_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-bauhinia-variegata-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 485676 B, 1512×1008 px, artifact_sha256 5a38587e481dd1f33401575320542b13e2b3ddc508ba12df428a1454b16c15b9 (sha256 5a38587e481dd1f33401575320542b13e2b3ddc508ba12df428a1454b16c15b9), spec_fingerprint 68eb58e3e0bb1a60ce52a1d3e30e4b90290cf6fbeabcbc36606d815cdc1da28e. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 68eb58e3e0bb1a60ce52a1d3e30e4b90290cf6fbeabcbc36606d815cdc1da28e; artifact_sha256: 5a38587e481dd1f33401575320542b13e2b3ddc508ba12df428a1454b16c15b9; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/bauhinia_variegata_turing_wavelength_s0/bauhinia_variegata_specimen.jpg=300694d305567ca5..., datasets/bauhinia_variegata_turing_wavelength_s0/bauhinia_variegata_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=65eb5aab368642b9...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-bauhinia-variegata-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) gives k_c and the requirement that the inhibitor diffuse faster. Schnakenberg (1979) gives the kinetics. Maini, Painter & Chau (1997) and Kondo & Miura (2010) review spatial wavelength selection. | Armon et al. (2011) is the centimetre-scale shell law for this species. Along 1 cm the 69.12 µm mode repeats 144 times and a 145th does not fit. Both are present at 0 Ma. This chronoseries has no earlier point.; reconstructed_in_script: D_u = 44.827 µm²/time and D_v = 16.9 D_u place the linear wavelength at 69.12 µm. A pure-mode integration gives sigma = 0.193 against the analytic 0.188. The saturated radial peak is 76.16 µm. | The adult frame is the MHNT photograph with a 42 percent blend of the activator in a corner inset. Full-frame Pearson r = 0.9935, valve RMSE = 2.42 gray levels, valve KS = 0.035.; transfer_boundary: The silhouette, seeds, and 1 cm bar are measured on the scan. The PDE does not grow the legume. The scan cannot show a 0.26 px wavelength, so the cellular field is the inset, not a texture painted across the valve at the wrong scale.; does_not_claim: Does not claim Bauhinia pericarp was measured at 69.12 µm in any cited paper. | Does not claim the 10 percent nonlinear shift (76.16 versus 69.12 µm) has been removed. | Does not claim the full-frame KS of 0.745 is a valve mismatch. It is the GIF palette moving the paper white. | Does not claim a second assessor or a signed nanopublication. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is present.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Full-frame KS remains 0.745 because the GIF palette moves the paper white. A lossless frame store would separate that artifact from the valve. The required product is a GIF.",
        "remediation needed: No blinded second assessor has scored this audit.",
        "remediation needed: The saturated radial wavelength is 76.16 µm rather than the linear 69.12 µm. A weakly nonlinear amplitude equation could account for the shift; it is not fitted away." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.73e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

